#
# sources - Windows 2000 DDK build description for xhci98.sys, the successor
# host controller driver (design record 13; roadmap-hcd.md).
#
# Build with scripts\build-driver.cmd, which runs the gates after every link.
# Output: src\objfre\i386\xhci98.sys (release), src\objchk\i386 (debug),
# src\objchk_qemu\i386 (qemu), and the amd64 trees beside them - build.exe
# appends the architecture and the wrapper overrides BUILD_ALT_DIR back to the
# flavour name (design record 11 section 8).
#
# SINCE 2026-10-02 THIS DIRECTORY IS THE HCD. The usbport miniport that
# xhci98.sys was until 1.2.0.0 left the tree that day (owner); its last
# sources are on branch 1.2.0.0 and its binaries in releases\1.2.0.0. The HCD
# links no usbport import library and imports nothing from usbport.sys - it
# replaces it - and the import gate refuses any USBPORT.SYS pair by name.
#
# THE PURE CORE (roadmap-hcd.md, "The shape of the successor", the "Lifted"
# row): ring, context, capability, port, memory carve, topology, descriptor
# and log code, DDK-free, with its host suites in test\ (design record 03).
# None of these files may grow an include of a file that needs ntddk.h. Three
# of them include xhci_usbport.h for its DDK-free type declarations and xhci.h
# still carries the miniport's extension layout; 26-A.2 carves both down to
# what the HCD uses.
#
# NOT BUILT, and kept as Phase 26's starting material: the roadmap's "Adapted"
# files - xhci_init.c, xhci_cmd.c, xhci_evt.c, xhci_pci.c - whose controller
# sequence, command engine and event drain the FDO of 26-A.2 keeps once their
# usbport service calls are replaced, and xhci_dbg.c, the qemu flavour's
# port-0xE9 trace channel. Each joins this list in the task that adapts it.
#
# Task 25.8's scaffold: the core plus a DriverEntry that registers nothing
# (hcd_entry.c). With nothing calling the core yet, /OPT:REF drops it from the
# image; the build still compiles every file and links them.
#

TARGETNAME=xhci98
TARGETTYPE=DRIVER
TARGETPATH=obj

INCLUDES=$(BASEDIR)\inc;$(BASEDIR)\inc\ddk

SOURCES=xhci_mem.c    \
        xhci_ring.c   \
        xhci_caps.c   \
        xhci_port.c   \
        xhci_ctx.c    \
        xhci_topo.c   \
        xhci_desc.c   \
        xhci_log.c    \
        hcd_entry.c   \
        hcd_pnp.c     \
        hcd_power.c   \
        xhci98.rc

#
# No diagnostic builds yet. The miniport's XHCI_EXTRA_DEFINES hatch existed for
# its probe and failed-start artifacts, which left with it; a value reaching
# this build would make an image no gate knows how to judge, so it is refused
# here - which also binds a bare `build` from a DDK prompt.
#
!IF "$(XHCI_EXTRA_DEFINES)" != ""
!ERROR XHCI_EXTRA_DEFINES is set, and xhci98.sys has no diagnostic builds since the HCD replaced the miniport (2026-10-02). Clear it before building.
!ENDIF

#
# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# The three build flavours (roadmap task 13-L.1, design record 08)
# ------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# BUILD_ALT_DIR is the DDK's own flavour discriminator: build.exe concatenates
# it onto `obj` to make the output tree, and setenv.bat sets it to fre or chk.
# scripts\build-driver.cmd overrides it to chk_qemu for the third flavour,
# because debug and qemu are both checked builds and would otherwise share
# src\objchk. The value may be at most 10 characters (build.exe's own limit).
#
#   release  BUILD_ALT_DIR=fre       free     ships, default
#   debug    BUILD_ALT_DIR=chk       checked  ships, the diagnostic download
#   qemu     BUILD_ALT_DIR=chk_qemu  checked  never published
#
# XHCI_DBG_LIVE and XHCI_DBG_E9 make the qemu flavour: the live trace and its
# port-0xE9 mirror, a runtime and a load-time hazard respectively on Windows 98
# metal (design record 08 section 5.1), both opt-in. XHCI_FLAVOUR_* is the
# in-image flavour marker hcd_entry.c emits.
#
!IF "$(BUILD_ALT_DIR)" == "chk_qemu"
C_DEFINES=$(C_DEFINES) -DXHCI_DBG_LIVE -DXHCI_DBG_E9 -DXHCI_FLAVOUR_QEMU
!ELSEIF "$(BUILD_ALT_DIR)" == "chk"
C_DEFINES=$(C_DEFINES) -DXHCI_FLAVOUR_DEBUG
!ELSEIF "$(BUILD_ALT_DIR)" == "fre"
C_DEFINES=$(C_DEFINES) -DXHCI_FLAVOUR_RELEASE
!ELSE
!ERROR BUILD_ALT_DIR is "$(BUILD_ALT_DIR)" and this tree knows exactly three flavours - fre (release), chk (debug) and chk_qemu (qemu). setenv.bat sets the first two; scripts\build-driver.cmd sets the third. A build with any other value would carry no flavour marker, so it is refused here rather than shipped as an unidentifiable binary.
!ENDIF

#
# No separate .rdata section, as the shipping NUSB/SP4 drivers and the
# miniport before this.
#
LINKER_FLAGS=-merge:.rdata=.text
